        "original_id": "5fbea633-364e-5047-9104-f8ebd2cd6463",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Runaway Scrape, Battle of San Jacinto\n- People: Sam Houston, Antonio López de Santa Anna\n- Organizations: Texian Army, Mexican Army of Operations, Mexican army\n- Places: Texas\n- Topics: Texas Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- The Runaway Scrape took place mainly between September 1835 and April 1836 in Texas during the Texas Revolution.\n- The Runaway Scrape was the evacuation of Texas residents fleeing the Mexican Army of Operations.\n- The Runaway Scrape spanned the period from the Battle of the Alamo through the Battle of San Jacinto.\n- At the Battle of San Jacinto, General Sam Houston led the Texian Army to defeat General Antonio López de Santa Anna's Mexican army.\n- The fight at the Battle of San Jacinto lasted 18 minutes.",
